---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import Showcase from "../../../components/Showcase.astro";

const install = `pnpm add @skryensya/core @skryensya/vanilla @skryensya/react`;

const html = `<div
  class="sk-segmented"
  data-sk-segmented
  data-value="day"
  role="radiogroup"
  aria-label="Rango"
>
  <span class="sk-segmented__indicator" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <button
    class="sk-segmented__option sk-interactive"
    data-sk-segmented-option
    data-value="day"
    type="button"
    role="radio"
  >
    Day
  </button>
  <button
    class="sk-segmented__option sk-interactive"
    data-sk-segmented-option
    data-value="week"
    type="button"
    role="radio"
  >
    Week
  </button>
  <button
    class="sk-segmented__option sk-interactive"
    data-sk-segmented-option
    data-value="month"
    type="button"
    role="radio"
  >
    Month
  </button>
</div>`;

const react = `import { SegmentedControl } from "@skryensya/react/segmented";

<SegmentedControl
  aria-label="Rango"
  defaultValue="day"
  onValueChange={setRange}
  options={[
    { value: "day", label: "Day" },
    { value: "week", label: "Week" },
    { value: "month", label: "Month" },
  ]}
/>;`;

const js = `import { initComponents } from "@skryensya/vanilla/auto";

await initComponents();`;
---

<Base title="SegmentedControl" description="SegmentedControl: unique and visible choice over a small group, with radiogroup semantics.">
  <h1>SegmentedControl</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    SegmentedControl is a single choice from a small, fixed set, displayed at once: a
    radiogroup with button bar clothes. To navigate between panels use
    <a href="/en/components/tabs">Tabs</a>; for many options or free text,
    <a href="/en/components/select">Select</a>.
  </p>

  <Showcase html={html} react={react} label="SegmentedControl" />
  <p>
    The vanilla enhancer selects with click and arrows; <code>Home</code> and <code>End</code> jump
    to the first and last segment. The chosen option is <code>data-value</code> and is announced with
    <code>aria-checked</code>. Each segment paints <code>--size-control-sm</code> and retains one hit
    from <code>44px</code> via <code>::after</code> (indicator follows painted case).
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={install} label="terminal" />

  <h2>Initialize vanilla</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={js} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of the preview. It is controlled (<code>value</code>) or uncontrolled (<code>defaultValue</code>); When changing, the indicator aligns and travels to the new option with the state change motion token.</p>
</Base>
